opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "Virtual package for the Linux kernel headers, which zig ships"
description: """
Zig ships the Linux UAPI headers (`linux/stddef.h`, `linux/fs.h`,
`linux/seccomp.h`, ...), so the build machine does not need a system
linux-libc-dev. Unlike conf-linux-libc-dev, which preprocesses a test with
the system's `cc`, this package is an empty check."""
maintainer: "Markus W. Weissmann <markus.weissmann@in.tum.de>"
authors: ["Markus W. Weissmann <markus.weissmann@in.tum.de>"]
homepage: "https://kernel.org/"
bug-reports: "https://github.com/ocaml/opam-repository/issues"
license: ["GPL-2.0-only"]
available: [os = "linux"]
build: []
flags: conf
